From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Start the primary client with vfork

The child only clears its signal mask, closes the pipe's read end and execs,
so vfork does, and it is the only way to start a process on a machine
without an MMU.  POSIX.1-2008 dropped vfork, so _DEFAULT_SOURCE asks for it
beside _POSIX_C_SOURCE.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Upstream: not submitted

--- a/cage.c
+++ b/cage.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
  */
 
 #define _POSIX_C_SOURCE 200112L
+#define _DEFAULT_SOURCE /* vfork(), which POSIX.1-2008 dropped */
 
 #include "config.h"
 
@@ -141,7 +142,9 @@
 		return false;
 	}
 
-	pid_t pid = fork();
+	/* The child only clears its signal mask and execs, so vfork does; it is all
+	   a machine without an MMU has. */
+	pid_t pid = vfork();
 	if (pid == 0) {
 		sigset_t set;
 		sigemptyset(&set);
